WEBVTT

00:00:01.240 --> 00:00:03.460
An additional order of 5,000 copies?

00:00:03.460 --> 00:00:04.190
<i>Yeah!</i>

00:00:04.190 --> 00:00:07.860
<i>Apparently the first 1,000 copies were sold out in an instant!</i>

00:00:07.860 --> 00:00:10.570
<i>The shops are pushing it really hard, too!</i>

00:00:10.570 --> 00:00:14.360
We regained in an instant what we lost at the winter Comiket, didn't we?

00:00:14.360 --> 00:00:17.350
<i>When people found out that
Kashiwagi Eri was making the art,</i>

00:00:17.350 --> 00:00:19.290
<i>it quickly got a lot of attention.</i>

00:00:19.860 --> 00:00:22.800
It's not like we were hiding it, though.

00:00:22.800 --> 00:00:27.800
<i>And after that, Kasumi Utako's scenario got a ton of praise on the internet!</i>

00:00:27.800 --> 00:00:29.570
That reeks of stealth marketing.

00:00:29.570 --> 00:00:31.550
Mainly by her.

00:00:31.550 --> 00:00:36.550
<i>Is that what you say about a comrade whom you've made a game with?</i>

00:00:36.550 --> 00:00:38.070
That was a joke!

00:00:38.070 --> 00:00:42.510
I just meant to say that the scenario is your achievement, too.

00:00:42.510 --> 00:00:45.600
<i>Well, the route I wrote has its ups and downs.</i>

00:00:45.600 --> 00:00:48.380
It's fine, I like it.

00:00:48.380 --> 00:00:50.370
<i>Y-Yeah...</i>

00:00:50.370 --> 00:00:51.610
<i>A-Anyway,</i>

00:00:51.920 --> 00:00:54.610
<i>this means that we're just getting started!</i>

00:00:54.610 --> 00:00:58.250
<i>Cherry Blessing is receiving more and more interest!</i>

00:00:58.250 --> 00:00:59.320
<i>Which means...</i>

00:00:59.320 --> 00:01:00.900
I got it!

00:01:00.900 --> 00:01:03.120
A "thank you to our fans" illustration, right?

00:01:03.120 --> 00:01:05.140
I'm drawing one now.

00:01:05.140 --> 00:01:06.140
<i>Yeah!</i>

00:01:06.140 --> 00:01:08.080
<i>On the same day the shops get the next batch,</i>

00:01:08.080 --> 00:01:10.860
<i>we change our main page to create even more buzz!</i>

00:01:10.860 --> 00:01:11.810
Tomoya,

00:01:11.810 --> 00:01:15.110
you're doing things exactly like Hashima right now!

00:01:18.300 --> 00:01:21.080
All right then, I'm about to add the finishing touches.

00:01:21.080 --> 00:01:23.770
Sure, I'm looking forward to seeing the completed illustration.

00:01:24.160 --> 00:01:25.230
Later.

00:01:33.960 --> 00:01:34.820
Oh?

00:01:36.020 --> 00:01:37.070
Huh?

00:01:37.690 --> 00:01:39.640
That's strange...

00:03:19.270 --> 00:03:20.720
Morning, Morals-kun.

00:03:20.720 --> 00:03:21.610
Oh.

00:03:22.720 --> 00:03:25.960
I heard you got an additional order for the game?

00:03:25.960 --> 00:03:26.720
Congratulations.

00:03:26.720 --> 00:03:29.100
T-Thank you very much!

00:03:29.100 --> 00:03:33.100
It seems I'll finally be able to compensate you properly for your work.

00:03:33.100 --> 00:03:34.610
I'm fine.

00:03:34.610 --> 00:03:36.900
It is just a students' circle, after all.

00:03:36.900 --> 00:03:37.640
No,

00:03:37.640 --> 00:03:41.150
precisely because it is a circle, we have to split the profits with everybody!

00:03:41.150 --> 00:03:45.700
Morals-kun, you're the circle representative and the producer.

00:03:45.700 --> 00:03:48.220
A con man and human garbage, so to speak.

00:03:48.220 --> 00:03:52.120
Why are you not keeping the profits for yourself, blowing it all on wild merrymaking,

00:03:52.120 --> 00:03:55.920
and still pretend to be fighting onward, earning the antipathy of your staff?

00:03:56.240 --> 00:03:58.050
I've meant to ask this for a long time,

00:03:58.050 --> 00:04:01.200
but did something happen between you and a producer?

00:04:03.670 --> 00:04:08.630
Come to think of it, Utaha-senpai, it's quite rare that you call out to me on our way to school.

00:04:08.630 --> 00:04:10.560
Is that so?

00:04:10.560 --> 00:04:15.310
Thinking about it, I feel like it hasn't happened even once in two years...

00:04:15.310 --> 00:04:17.930
I'm graduating soon.

00:04:19.640 --> 00:04:21.820
I can't be with you any more, either.

00:04:23.100 --> 00:04:24.760
That's why...

00:04:24.760 --> 00:04:29.430
I want to burn the road to school we walked together for three years into my memory.

00:04:31.150 --> 00:04:32.960
With you...

00:04:32.960 --> 00:04:34.330
Like this...

00:04:34.330 --> 00:04:36.330
Utaha-senpa-

00:04:38.530 --> 00:04:40.120
Tomoya!

00:04:40.120 --> 00:04:44.110
Why did you leave me behind when I came all the way to your house to walk with you?!

00:04:44.110 --> 00:04:47.640
You have never done anything like that in the last eight years!

00:04:47.640 --> 00:04:50.640
The circumstances were different before!

00:04:50.640 --> 00:04:51.550
My,

00:04:51.550 --> 00:04:54.360
I wonder how exactly your circumstances have changed.

00:04:54.360 --> 00:04:56.000
T-That's...

00:04:56.000 --> 00:04:56.970
For example,

00:04:56.970 --> 00:05:00.010
Sawamura-san, did you take  responsibility for failing the winter Comiket,

00:05:00.010 --> 00:05:02.180
and make yourself Morals-kun's slave,

00:05:02.180 --> 00:05:08.280
serving beside him like this on the road to school, the classroom, and all the way to his bed?

00:05:09.010 --> 00:05:13.070
A-A gloomy preying woman like you, who says she wants to make memories before graduating,

00:05:13.070 --> 00:05:17.490
but actually intends to create that reality by herself, shouldn't say anything to me!

00:05:17.490 --> 00:05:19.200
Calm down, you two!

00:05:19.200 --> 00:05:21.810
You're destroying the reputation you've been creating until now!

00:05:21.810 --> 00:05:23.480
That's right, Sawamura-san.

00:05:23.480 --> 00:05:25.420
Me aside, are you okay with it?

00:05:25.860 --> 00:05:29.720
You're revealing the shameful fact that you're not only an otaku and an ero-doujin author,

00:05:29.720 --> 00:05:31.940
but an irredeemable loser, too.

00:05:31.940 --> 00:05:35.180
I'm an otaku and an ero-doujin author, but not a loser!

00:05:35.180 --> 00:05:36.910
Stop that already!

00:05:36.910 --> 00:05:40.640
If you clamour like this where people are watching...

00:05:40.640 --> 00:05:42.110
Tomoya!

00:05:42.110 --> 00:05:44.820
What's that about?!

00:05:44.820 --> 00:05:47.990
...guys who get the wrong idea like this will appear.

00:05:48.640 --> 00:05:52.390
Pinned between Sawamura-san and Kasumigaoka-senpai...

00:05:52.390 --> 00:05:53.450
Is that it?!

00:05:53.450 --> 00:05:57.010
Did you become the main character of a school harem love comedy?!

00:05:57.010 --> 00:05:58.010
Whoa,

00:05:58.010 --> 00:06:04.260
I think I just understood how annoying school harem love comedies' main characters' best friend characters can be.

00:06:04.260 --> 00:06:05.400
Damn you!

00:06:05.400 --> 00:06:09.400
Revealing such a bomb before Valentine's Day next month...

00:06:09.400 --> 00:06:11.610
Oh, morning, Katou.

00:06:11.610 --> 00:06:12.730
Morning.

00:06:12.730 --> 00:06:14.360
Morning, Katou-san.

00:06:20.200 --> 00:06:22.110
H-Hey, Katou.

00:06:22.110 --> 00:06:25.320
The next circle meeting is this Friday.

00:06:25.320 --> 00:06:26.580
I see.

00:06:26.580 --> 00:06:28.160
Since you haven't come for-

00:06:28.160 --> 00:06:30.470
The class is starting, Aki-kun.

00:06:32.270 --> 00:06:33.230
Yeah.

00:06:35.170 --> 00:06:36.120
Look now!

00:06:36.120 --> 00:06:41.340
Thanks to that flashy popular guy event, your real wife is grumpy.

00:06:43.480 --> 00:06:47.380
No, that's not it.

00:06:50.140 --> 00:06:54.310
<i>It's not anything that simple.</i>

00:06:56.500 --> 00:06:57.890
And so, Tomoya-kun,

00:06:58.630 --> 00:07:00.180
it's a bit early,

00:07:00.180 --> 00:07:03.900
but would you accept this Valentine's chocolate?

00:07:03.900 --> 00:07:04.810
No, no, no, wait!

00:07:04.810 --> 00:07:06.270
Wait a minute, Iori!

00:07:06.270 --> 00:07:09.080
You don't have to be that much against it!

00:07:09.080 --> 00:07:10.860
We're former best friends, aren't we?

00:07:13.020 --> 00:07:19.220
Well, I do admit that I intentionally failed to mention that Izumi asked me to give this to you.

00:07:19.220 --> 00:07:21.480
Stop with all those stupid jokes!

00:07:21.480 --> 00:07:24.560
It seems that she wanted to give it to you herself,

00:07:24.560 --> 00:07:28.420
but unfortunately the prefectural schools' entrance exams are getting close, so she's very busy.

00:07:28.420 --> 00:07:29.660
I see.

00:07:29.660 --> 00:07:31.760
So Izumi-chan is going to a prefectural school.

00:07:32.090 --> 00:07:34.410
Tell her to do her best.

00:07:34.410 --> 00:07:36.330
So, what about you?

00:07:36.330 --> 00:07:37.640
Are you doing your best?

00:07:37.640 --> 00:07:39.240
With what?

00:07:39.240 --> 00:07:40.670
My finals?

00:07:40.670 --> 00:07:42.770
Your next game, of course.

00:07:42.770 --> 00:07:45.400
Have you signed up for summer Comiket yet?

00:07:46.200 --> 00:07:48.860
It's problematic for me if you don't.

00:07:49.480 --> 00:07:51.860
To settle the issue for good, too.

00:07:51.860 --> 00:07:53.250
Iori?

00:07:53.250 --> 00:07:55.250
After your game hit the stores,

00:07:55.250 --> 00:07:58.330
our competition became a full-on rivalry.

00:07:58.330 --> 00:08:01.000
Our sales are still higher,

00:08:01.830 --> 00:08:05.500
but people's opinions seem to be heading in the other direction.

00:08:05.500 --> 00:08:07.010
Of course!

00:08:07.010 --> 00:08:10.260
We have Kashiwagi Eri and Kasumi Utako!

00:08:10.260 --> 00:08:13.260
Content-wise, we'll never lose!

00:08:13.260 --> 00:08:15.610
Even so, I thought we could win.

00:08:15.610 --> 00:08:20.020
No, if they had been like before, we would've had a chance.

00:08:20.850 --> 00:08:24.330
But with this game, they've matured a lot.

00:08:24.330 --> 00:08:28.220
The scenario and the art both gave us a blow like nothing before.

00:08:28.220 --> 00:08:30.530
So you did play the game.

00:08:31.010 --> 00:08:32.430
Not just me.

00:08:32.430 --> 00:08:35.480
Everybody in our circle played it.

00:08:35.480 --> 00:08:37.030
It got huge praise.

00:08:37.030 --> 00:08:39.240
I-I see.

00:08:39.240 --> 00:08:41.290
Thanks, I suppose.

00:08:41.290 --> 00:08:42.370
You're welcome!

00:08:43.570 --> 00:08:46.880
Well, I guess you may get some resentment afterwards.

00:08:46.880 --> 00:08:48.470
What do you mean?

00:08:49.130 --> 00:08:53.550
I revealed that you cooperated on the scenario.

00:08:54.040 --> 00:08:57.740
The perfectly happy end of the last route...

00:08:57.740 --> 00:08:59.790
You wrote that, didn't you?

00:08:59.790 --> 00:09:01.560
Well noticed.

00:09:01.560 --> 00:09:09.320
You know, I have the LitRhap 2 book you and Izumi made three years ago, of which only five copies exist.

00:09:12.550 --> 00:09:16.940
Your style hasn't changed at all from back then, Tomoya-kun!

00:09:16.940 --> 00:09:19.440
Maybe you could even say you haven't matured at all!

00:09:20.110 --> 00:09:21.480
I'll give you 5,000 yen!

00:09:21.480 --> 00:09:22.260
I will!

00:09:22.260 --> 00:09:25.040
Let me hide that dark piece of history!

00:09:25.870 --> 00:09:27.880
Well then, I'm leaving now.

00:09:27.880 --> 00:09:29.000
Are we clear?

00:09:29.000 --> 00:09:31.840
Don't ever show that book to anyone.

00:09:33.790 --> 00:09:34.930
Hey, Tomoya-kun.

00:09:34.930 --> 00:09:36.270
What is it?

00:09:36.270 --> 00:09:38.590
Are you holding on to more of my secrets?

00:09:38.950 --> 00:09:41.710
Summer Comiket or winter Comiket, whichever is fine.

00:09:41.710 --> 00:09:43.600
Continue your circle.

00:09:43.600 --> 00:09:45.100
Huh?

00:09:45.100 --> 00:09:48.800
Don't lose the place you belong.

00:09:48.800 --> 00:09:51.110
Y-You don't have to tell me!

00:09:51.710 --> 00:09:57.120
Don't let go of those two... Kashiwagi Eri and Kasumi Utako.

00:09:57.780 --> 00:09:58.750
Iori?

00:10:05.620 --> 00:10:08.620
A new game, huh?

00:10:09.130 --> 00:10:12.130
<i>Can I really make one?</i>

00:10:12.460 --> 00:10:17.130
<i>Can I interfere more with Utaha-senpai's work as an author?</i>

00:10:18.430 --> 00:10:22.270
<i>Can I push Eriri to do more unreasonable things?</i>

00:10:45.990 --> 00:10:46.960
<i>Hey,</i>

00:10:47.760 --> 00:10:49.630
<i>what do you think I should do?</i>

00:10:53.100 --> 00:10:53.960
Here,

00:10:53.960 --> 00:10:55.250
chocolate.

00:10:56.550 --> 00:10:57.760
What, what's wrong?

00:10:58.480 --> 00:11:02.320
Is it perhaps your first time ever
getting Valentine's Day chocolate?

00:11:02.320 --> 00:11:03.500
N-No,

00:11:03.500 --> 00:11:07.750
I'm just surprised that you're not following your usual tsundere pattern.

00:11:07.750 --> 00:11:08.640
What's that?

00:11:09.040 --> 00:11:10.480
Well, normally you'd say...

00:11:10.480 --> 00:11:14.180
"I didn't get this chocolate for you, so don't get the wrong idea!"

00:11:14.180 --> 00:11:15.830
...while giving it to me, right?

00:11:15.830 --> 00:11:18.740
What do you think I am?

00:11:19.710 --> 00:11:20.860
And also,

00:11:21.430 --> 00:11:24.870
this is the second time I get chocolate from you.

00:11:24.870 --> 00:11:26.640
It's been nine years.

00:11:27.970 --> 00:11:29.360
W-What are you saying?

00:11:29.360 --> 00:11:31.240
Yes, that's the reaction!

00:11:31.240 --> 00:11:37.600
That's the calculated tsun to dere pattern we moefags yearn for!

00:11:37.600 --> 00:11:39.380
Whatever.

00:11:39.750 --> 00:11:44.540
I see... so you've agreed to meet Kasumigaoka Utaha for lunch.

00:11:44.540 --> 00:11:45.370
Yeah!

00:11:45.370 --> 00:11:48.580
Because Kasumi Utako's new book was finally released.

00:11:48.580 --> 00:11:51.980
She has to be the very first one I tell my impressions to!

00:11:51.980 --> 00:11:55.590
Good job creating a reason on Valentine's Day...

00:11:55.590 --> 00:11:58.700
Eriri, you should just read Kasumi Utako too.

00:11:58.700 --> 00:12:00.070
So that we can talk about it.

00:12:00.070 --> 00:12:02.620
I've read it three times already.

00:12:02.620 --> 00:12:06.730
It's once again full of Kasumi Utako's characteristic style!

00:12:06.730 --> 00:12:09.400
Of course the writing ability
and the power to draw you in-

00:12:09.400 --> 00:12:13.580
Oh no, I was supposed to tell her first!

00:12:14.380 --> 00:12:17.270
So, Megumi's obligatory chocolate too...

00:12:17.270 --> 00:12:19.570
You're getting a great harvest this Valentine's Day.

00:12:20.660 --> 00:12:22.050
What's that reaction?

00:12:22.050 --> 00:12:24.860
You still haven't made up?!

00:12:24.860 --> 00:12:25.960
Q-Quiet.

00:12:25.960 --> 00:12:27.680
It's been almost two months!

00:12:28.230 --> 00:12:31.830
Hasn't it come to the point where you could say you two have run your natural course?

00:12:31.830 --> 00:12:33.340
Does it look like that?

00:12:33.340 --> 00:12:35.520
You really think so?!

00:12:35.520 --> 00:12:37.360
If you're that worried,

00:12:37.360 --> 00:12:39.820
would you like me to contact Megumi?

00:12:39.820 --> 00:12:42.410
N-No, it's all right.

00:12:42.410 --> 00:12:46.870
This is a problem I have to solve by myself.

00:12:47.710 --> 00:12:51.870
But if it was caused by the winter Comiket thing, I'm responsible for it too...

00:12:51.870 --> 00:12:54.890
You're not responsible for it in the slightest!

00:12:54.890 --> 00:12:56.050
Tomoya...

00:12:56.750 --> 00:12:58.480
More importantly, Eriri...

00:12:58.480 --> 00:13:02.030
Um, you know, worry about the special illustrations.

00:13:04.250 --> 00:13:05.160
What?

00:13:05.160 --> 00:13:06.810
You don't want to do it?

00:13:06.810 --> 00:13:09.260
That's not it, but...

00:13:09.900 --> 00:13:12.770
But perhaps you could wait a little longer.

00:13:12.770 --> 00:13:16.470
Well, it's not like it's something we've announced already,

00:13:16.470 --> 00:13:18.440
so there's no particular hurry.

00:13:18.440 --> 00:13:20.120
So a little longer!

00:13:20.120 --> 00:13:23.780
I think holding off a little will increase my motivation.

00:13:23.780 --> 00:13:26.030
If that's the case, let's start with two weeks!

00:13:26.030 --> 00:13:27.780
I mean,

00:13:28.150 --> 00:13:31.040
let's do away with such deadlines.

00:13:31.320 --> 00:13:34.280
Let's not talk about those for now.

00:13:34.280 --> 00:13:35.340
Eriri?

00:13:36.620 --> 00:13:39.660
Could you let me take it easy for a little longer?

00:13:40.290 --> 00:13:42.800
I did so much before.

00:13:46.110 --> 00:13:49.930
Well, you can draw it whenever you feel like it.

00:13:53.650 --> 00:13:55.120
By the way, Tomoya.

00:13:55.120 --> 00:13:58.080
Where will you and Kasumigaoka Utaha be having your date?

00:13:58.080 --> 00:14:01.340
If you tell me honestly what you will do with that information,

00:14:01.340 --> 00:14:03.360
I might be inclined to answer.

00:14:04.440 --> 00:14:06.400
So, Kasumi-sensei,

00:14:06.400 --> 00:14:09.570
congratulations on releasing Pure Love Hectopascal!

00:14:10.140 --> 00:14:11.310
Thank you.

00:14:11.940 --> 00:14:14.060
Well, it was a little late, though.

00:14:14.060 --> 00:14:16.910
I pulled an all-nighter last night, and read it three times!

00:14:16.910 --> 00:14:20.630
Yeah, Kasumi Utako hasn't changed in the least!

00:14:20.630 --> 00:14:25.990
Well, of course, I feel like the writing ability and the power to draw you in are even more formidable than before,

00:14:25.990 --> 00:14:30.400
but honestly, me talking about the technique isn't going to convince anyone.

00:14:30.400 --> 00:14:33.690
More importantly, should I say the atmosphere, or the ambience, of the story...

00:14:33.690 --> 00:14:37.080
It is very much like Kasumi Utako!

00:14:38.550 --> 00:14:40.710
You're the same as always, Morals-kun.

00:14:40.710 --> 00:14:43.070
I'll definitely come to the signing event next week!

00:14:43.070 --> 00:14:44.640
I'll be the very first one in line...

00:14:44.640 --> 00:14:45.830
If that's what you want,

00:14:45.830 --> 00:14:49.530
I can do it right here and now.

00:14:49.530 --> 00:14:51.120
N-No...

00:14:51.120 --> 00:14:53.960
I don't want to get the autograph from Utaha-senpai, my acquaintance,

00:14:53.960 --> 00:14:56.820
but Kasumi Utako the author.

00:14:56.820 --> 00:14:57.820
Is that so?

00:14:57.820 --> 00:15:01.170
So I'll put in my signature as Kasumigaoka Utaha now, then.

00:15:01.700 --> 00:15:03.730
On your body, that is.

00:15:05.420 --> 00:15:09.760
Stop with those jokes when you're calling me Morals-kun!

00:15:10.440 --> 00:15:13.140
Well, even if that's a joke,

00:15:13.140 --> 00:15:15.890
I'll have to give this to you today.

00:15:16.630 --> 00:15:17.670
Seriously?

00:15:17.670 --> 00:15:20.480
What are you saying about something this small at this point?

00:15:20.480 --> 00:15:23.270
Even though we're close enough to have spent many a night together.

00:15:23.270 --> 00:15:26.000
Writing the plot and the scenario, that is!

00:15:27.470 --> 00:15:30.110
But I'm glad I could give it to you today.

00:15:30.110 --> 00:15:33.440
Starting tomorrow, I won't be coming to school any more.

00:15:34.130 --> 00:15:35.540
I see.

00:15:35.540 --> 00:15:38.290
Your university and graduation were confirmed already.

00:15:38.610 --> 00:15:40.760
I also have to write the second volume.

00:15:40.760 --> 00:15:44.680
I have to fully concentrate on that before the university starts.

00:15:45.760 --> 00:15:47.960
So, Utaha-senpai,

00:15:47.960 --> 00:15:50.900
what will you do after starting university?

00:15:51.850 --> 00:15:56.100
Well, Pure Love Hectopascal will go on for a while.

00:15:56.100 --> 00:16:00.330
Machida-san is excited too, saying that this will be the one to get an anime adaptation.

00:16:00.330 --> 00:16:03.060
What about our circle?

00:16:03.060 --> 00:16:05.810
I won't ask anything as absurd as before, like doing all the routes.

00:16:05.810 --> 00:16:09.320
Just doing one route, or even an extra scenario,

00:16:09.320 --> 00:16:12.030
no matter how long it takes, will be fine...

00:16:12.460 --> 00:16:16.500
So would you participate in our next game too?

00:16:18.070 --> 00:16:22.100
Do you have an idea for the next game?

00:16:22.100 --> 00:16:23.290
Well...

00:16:24.060 --> 00:16:25.540
If I had a week!

00:16:25.540 --> 00:16:29.910
And if you're going to do a new game, who will do the art?

00:16:30.870 --> 00:16:33.050
Will you appoint Sawamura-san again?

00:16:33.050 --> 00:16:35.370
Can you do it as you are now?

00:16:36.090 --> 00:16:37.340
Have you noticed?

00:16:37.340 --> 00:16:41.250
That Sawamura-san hasn't drawn a single picture the entire year.

00:16:41.250 --> 00:16:43.060
She is drawing!

00:16:43.500 --> 00:16:47.180
She just doesn't like the results, so she keeps redoing them...

00:16:47.180 --> 00:16:51.140
It's already been a month since the initial deadline we agreed on.

00:16:51.140 --> 00:16:53.820
You can't call that drawing.

00:16:53.820 --> 00:16:57.700
I'm sure lots of artists would flip out if you told them that.

00:16:57.700 --> 00:17:02.700
The one allowing that is nobody else but you, Morals-kun.

00:17:03.000 --> 00:17:05.830
But she let it affect her health last year-

00:17:05.830 --> 00:17:07.930
But she has completely recovered.

00:17:07.930 --> 00:17:11.090
She had no other unavoidable circumstances.

00:17:11.090 --> 00:17:14.990
If she still can't draw, she can't participate in any production work.

00:17:17.240 --> 00:17:20.640
Why is she the only one you're so overprotective about?

00:17:20.640 --> 00:17:24.650
That may make Sawamura Eriri glad,

00:17:24.650 --> 00:17:27.970
but I don't think Kashiwagi Eri is happy.

00:17:27.970 --> 00:17:30.180
Utaha-senpai...

00:17:30.180 --> 00:17:35.320
If possible, I would like to work together with her again.

00:17:36.490 --> 00:17:44.670
Together with Kashiwagi Eri's pictures, I want to create a game which surpasses even Cherry Blessing.

00:17:47.590 --> 00:17:48.750
It looks like it's going to snow.

00:17:49.310 --> 00:17:51.700
Don't go anywhere on your way home!

00:18:19.070 --> 00:18:20.540
Seriously?

00:18:54.840 --> 00:18:55.780
Yes!

00:18:59.430 --> 00:19:01.910
<i>She saw it.</i>

00:19:30.780 --> 00:19:32.100
Huh...

00:19:32.690 --> 00:19:35.610
Her expression changed like this here?

00:19:38.470 --> 00:19:40.860
<i>It's not because I have to or because I have no choice.</i>

00:19:41.220 --> 00:19:45.030
<i>I seriously want to make a game.</i>

00:19:52.290 --> 00:19:55.040
<i>The direction sure is detailed.</i>

00:19:55.040 --> 00:19:57.420
<i>If you don't know without playing,</i>

00:19:57.420 --> 00:19:58.950
<i>then you just have to play it!</i>

00:19:58.950 --> 00:20:00.220
<i>It's the weekend, too!</i>

00:20:00.220 --> 00:20:01.340
<i>So let's include it.</i>

00:20:01.340 --> 00:20:02.520
<i>Take this.</i>

00:20:02.520 --> 00:20:05.870
<i>Let's make it playable before this week is up.</i>

00:20:06.760 --> 00:20:09.180
It is so well done.

00:20:10.750 --> 00:20:15.400
Why have you worked on this so hard, Katou?

00:20:47.040 --> 00:20:48.100
I'm sorry.

00:20:49.480 --> 00:20:51.840
I'm sorry, Katou.
